REM  pench.pni — the embodied cycler.  پیچ
REM  THE THING DESCRIBED HERE CAN MOVE AND CAN INJURE. That is why the
REM  envelope is not an optional field and why an unknown limit must be
REM  written "not established" rather than estimated.

CYCLER PENCH
  TITLE   "Pench"
  SCRIPT  "پیچ"
  OUTPUT  EMBODIED
  UNIT    "manoeuvre"
  PURPOSE "Put intent into the physical world: a robot, a cyberphysical system, factory automation, a digital twin, transfer in either direction between simulation and reality."

  CONTRACT
    REFUSE    "a manoeuvre with no stated operating envelope"
    REFUSE    "an invented limit in place of an unknown one"
    REFUSE    "a sim-to-real claim that names no hardware run"
    INVARIANT "an unknown limit is written not-established, never estimated"
    EVIDENCE  "what a run produced: a log, a bag file, a plot, a capture"
    EVIDENCE  "stated limits, or a stated absence of them"
  END CONTRACT

  STAGE MANOEUVRES
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT LIST
    INTO   manoeuvres
    ASK
      Embodied work, "{book}", on {platform}. Break it into manoeuvres.

      Reply with ONLY a JSON array, in the order they are performed:
      [{"title":"…","precondition":"…","beat":"…"}]

      precondition: what must already be true before it may start.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COUNT(manoeuvres) > 0
  END STAGE

  STAGE MOTION
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    REPEAT FOREACH manoeuvres
    INTO   manoeuvre.lead
    ASK
      Manoeuvre {manoeuvre.title} on {platform}.
      Precondition: {manoeuvre.precondition}

      ONE paragraph of 50 to 90 words: what the system does, in the vocabulary the work
      uses. Name the actuators and the sensors that matter.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ENVELOPE
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   MEASURE
    EXPECT TEXT
    INTO   manoeuvre.envelope
    ASK
      Same manoeuvre. State the operating envelope in 60 to 110 words. Be specific and
      refuse to guess:

      — the limits it must stay inside: reach, force, speed, torque, temperature, current
      — what is in range of it, including people, and how they are kept out
      — how it is stopped, by whom, and how quickly
      — what happens if power, network or a sensor is lost mid-manoeuvre
      — what it must NOT be run near

      Where a limit is not known, write "not established" rather than a plausible number.
      An invented limit is worse than an absent one.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NOT EMPTY(manoeuvre.envelope)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE GAP
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   VERIFY
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   manoeuvre.envelope
    INTO   manoeuvre.gap
    ASK
      Same manoeuvre. In 50 to 90 words: what ran in simulation, what ran on hardware,
      and where they disagreed. Name the disagreement rather than smoothing it — friction,
      latency, compliance, sensor noise, backlash, thermal drift.

      If it has only ever been simulated, say exactly that. Do not describe a transfer
      that has not happened.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NOT EMPTY(manoeuvre.gap)
  END STAGE

  STAGE PROOF
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   EXECUTE
    EXPECT ANY
    OPTIONAL
    ATTACH INBOX
    ASK
      Bring back what an actual run produced for {manoeuvre.title}: a log, a bag file,
      a plot, a capture. This is not generated — it is captured. Run it, record it,
      and bring it back through the inbox.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE ABSTRACT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    EXPECT TEXT
    FROM   manoeuvres
    INTO   book.description
    ASK
      Deposit abstract for "{book}", embodied work in {count} manoeuvres.
      Two or three HTML paragraphs in <p> tags.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE SAFETYGATE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB  VERIFY
    GATE  HUMAN "ENVELOPE reviewed"
    ENVELOPE "no manoeuvre publishes without a reviewed envelope"
  END STAGE

  STAGE MINT
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB  INTEGRATE
    GATE  HUMAN "MINT pench"
    EMIT  DOI
  END STAGE
END CYCLER
